course: dictionary
lesson: 11931
title: Words that carry a smell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you about smells as well as sights. Camphor is one of them. Use the clues around the word: «The old trunk smelled of camphor when Grandma opened the lid.» An old trunk that has been shut away and a smell that comes out when the lid opens tell you camphor is a strong, sharp smell.
explain: Camphor is also a thing you can hold. It is a white, waxy substance. «Grandad rubbed a little camphor rub on his sore back» tells you it is used in rubs that people put on their skin, but a rub is not a sweet or a drink.
explain: Clues can also warn you. «Keep the camphor bottle on the high shelf, away from little hands.» Keeping it up high and away from small children tells you it can harm you if swallowed. When a text warns you about something, pay close attention.
fact: Camphor is a white, waxy substance with a strong, sharp smell.
fact: Camphor is taken from the wood of the camphor tree, or it is made in factories.
fact: In the past, people kept moths away from clothes with camphor or mothballs.
fact: In science, camphor turns straight from a solid to a gas, which is why its smell spreads.
fact: Camphor is poisonous if swallowed, especially for small children.
exercise: «The old trunk smelled of camphor when Grandma opened the lid.» What is camphor? | A loud noise from the attic | *A white, waxy substance with a strong, sharp smell | A bright flower that grows in gardens | A soft blanket for winter
exercise: Which of these is true about where camphor comes from? | It is a shell found on the beach | *It can be taken from the wood of the camphor tree | It is grown as a sweet crop on farms | It falls from clouds like rain
exercise: «Keep the camphor bottle on the high shelf, away from little hands.» Why must it be kept away from little hands? | Camphor is too heavy for small hands to lift | Camphor is only for cooking food | Camphor makes people fall asleep at once | *Camphor is poisonous if swallowed
test: «Moths were kept away from the wool jumpers with camphor in the drawer.» What job did the camphor do? | *It kept moths away from clothes | It made the jumpers warm to wear | It turned the jumpers a bright colour | It washed the jumpers in water
test: «The camphor smell slowly spread through the whole room.» Why did the smell spread so well? | Camphor is heavier than air and sinks | *Camphor turns straight from a solid into a gas | Camphor was poured into the water pipes | Camphor was stuck to the carpet with glue
exam: Which statement about camphor is true and important to know? | It is a loud sound made by old machines | It is a sweet, so children can eat it safely | It only grows in very cold places | *It is poisonous if swallowed, especially for small children
